/Contents (The Streaming Systems book explains how streamingsystems reason about time, ordering, state, andcorrectness. Concepts like event time, processing time,watermarks, late data, and windowing are explainedclearly and rigorously. It focuses on how streaming systemsthink, not on how to use a specific framework. Once youunderstand these ideas, tools like Kafka Streams, Flink, orSpark Structured Streaming stop feeling mysterious.)
