634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (Designing Data Intensive Applications book breaks down the core building blocks of modern data systems: storage engines, replication, partitioning, consistency models, and stream processing. It explains why different systems make different tradeoffs and what those tradeoffs cost you in practice. You are not taught how to use a specific database. You are taught how databases and distributed systems work under the hood.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [323 0 R 324 0 R]
>>
endobj
635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 219 0 R
/E (The Streaming Systems book explains how streaming systems reason about time, ordering, state, and correctness. Concepts like event time, processing time, watermarks, late data, and windowing are explained clearly and rigorously. It focuses on how streaming systems think, not on how to use a specific framework. Once you understand these ideas, tools like Kafka Streams, Flink, or Spark Structured Streaming stop feeling mysterious.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [325 0 R]
>>
endobj
636 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (The Data Warehouse Toolkit book teaches dimensional modeling. Facts, dimensions, grain, slowly changing dimensions, and how to design tables that are stable, readable, and hard to misuse. This is the Kimball approach to dimensional modeling that remains the gold standard. It focuses on analytics systems, not raw ingestion or processing. You learn how to structure data so that business questions can be answered consistently without rewriting logic every time.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [326 0 R 327 0 R 328 0 R 329 0 R]
>>
endobj
637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (Data Engineering with Python book walks you through designing, building, and automating data pipelines using Python. It covers connecting to databases, building transformations, and working with orchestration tools like Airflow and NiFi. Many examples focus on real-world scenarios, giving you a chance to see the code and the context where it is useful.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [330 0 R 331 0 R 332 0 R 333 0 R]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Data Pipelines Pocket Reference book defines the common components of data pipelines, explains how data moves through ingestion, processing, and output, and highlights key decisions like batch versus streaming. It also touches on testing, maintenance, and alerting for reliable operations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [334 0 R 335 0 R]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (The Designing Cloud Data Platforms book explains how to architect data systems on cloud providers, covering ingestion, storage patterns, streaming, governance, and cost optimization. It also discusses multi-cloud strategies and real world pitfalls. You learn why you might choose a managed service for oracle-style workloads versus a serverless or open-source stack.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [336 0 R 337 0 R 338 0 R]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (This book is great in explaining Hadoop technology. Even though technology is not very popular on the SME level it argues that enterprise application is still viable. Interesting read focusing on practical use cases to create big data infrastructure both in the cloud and on-premises. It will be useful for seasoned data engineers tasked to create enterprise-level pipelines in the cloud and ensure a high level of security and availability.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [339 0 R]
>>
endobj
641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /L
/P 225 0 R
/K [848 0 R]
/Pg 18 0 R
>>
endobj
642 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (Analytics Engineering with SQL and dbt is a practical guide to building reliable, scalable, and well-documented analytics workflows using SQL and dbt. The book walks you through the principles of analytics engineering, showing how raw data can be transformed into trusted datasets that power reporting, dashboards, and business decision-making.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [341 0 R]
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (It covers essential topics such as data modeling, SQL transformations, testing, documentation, version control, and modular development with dbt. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [342 0 R]
>>
